#---
# purpose: "a process parked on a receive keeps everything the receive needs across a collection: the pinned list the matcher compares against, the clause body's captured values and the after body; a sender's matching message still wins afterwards"
#---
#
# The parent builds a 100-element list to pin and 200 cells of garbage within
# its first quantum, so nothing is collected before it parks and its heap is
# due at the park. The collection that follows the park moves the pinned list,
# the clause body closure that captured `kept` and the after body closure. The
# child then sends an equal list: its probe runs the matcher over the moved
# pinned list, wins, and the parent resumes in the clause body.
def main() do
  parent = self()
  key = Enum.to_list(1..100)
  kept = [:a, :b, :c]
  dbg(Enum.count(Enum.to_list(1..200)))
  spawn(fn () -> send(parent, Enum.to_list(1..100)) end)
  receive do
    ^key -> dbg(kept)
  after
    5000 -> dbg(:timeout)
  end
end
